#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Mewo Session for Linux: one build session of "Build with me" in a window
of its own.

The daemon writes this file next to its state and starts it with an info
file (JSON): the session's number, goal, feature, worktree, model, the
script to run and the daemon's socket. The script records its pid and then
becomes Claude Code, so the daemon tracks the run as it tracks a headless
one. The header follows the session: its state (working, needs you,
finished), its plan status and its pull request.

Two bodies. The chat (info "mode": "chat", needs WebKitGTK): Claude Code
runs in its stream mode (JSON lines on stdin and stdout) and the page
beside this file, mewo-session-chat.html, draws the conversation the way
the Claude Code extension does: messages, tool calls with input and output,
diffs, questions and permission prompts as buttons, a composer with the
model and the mode. A prompt that waits also goes to the phones, through
`mewo ask`, and the first answer wins. The terminal (GTK + VTE) is the
other body: Claude Code as it is in a terminal, in the console's colours;
it is what opens without WebKitGTK.

In the terminal, Ctrl+C copies the selection (with nothing selected it reaches Claude as
usual), Ctrl+V pastes text (an image on the clipboard goes to Claude, which
pastes it itself), Ctrl+Shift+C / Ctrl+Shift+V always copy and paste, a
right click offers Copy, Paste and Select all; Ctrl+= / Ctrl+- / Ctrl+0 zoom.
"""

